options.content:
The returned data should have columns of integer types for some visualizations to work properly.

Pie chart is one of them.

The backend tries to read the metadata from Thruk, and if it does not exist, it tries to infer the type.

The function query.go:determineTableFieldType determines the type

If first data instance is parsable as float64, the column is taken as float64 column. Otherwise it defaults to string.


### Thruk API Metadata

Here is the return value of the API call.

https://demo.thruk.org/demo/thruk/r/v1/services/totals

Without metadata:
```json
{
   "critical" : 0,
   "critical_and_unhandled" : 0,
   "ok" : 7,
   "pending" : 0,
   "total" : 8,
   "unknown" : 0,
   "unknown_and_unhandled" : 0,
   "warning" : 1,
   "warning_and_unhandled" : 1
}
```

Or with metadata:

```json
{
   "data" : {
      "critical" : 1,
      "critical_and_unhandled" : 1,
      "ok" : 7,
      "pending" : 0,
      "total" : 8,
      "unknown" : 0,
      "unknown_and_unhandled" : 0,
      "warning" : 0,
      "warning_and_unhandled" : 0
   },
   "meta" : {
      "columns" : [
         {
            "name" : "critical"
         },
         {
            "name" : "critical_and_unhandled"
         },
         {
            "name" : "ok"
         },
         {
            "name" : "pending"
         },
         {
            "name" : "total"
         },
         {
            "name" : "unknown"
         },
         {
            "name" : "unknown_and_unhandled"
         },
         {
            "name" : "warning"
         },
         {
            "name" : "warning_and_unhandled"
         }
      ]
   }
}
```

There is a PR open in Thruk to add type metadata to most of the API calls:

https://github.com/sni/thruk/pull/1507

### Force adding the known types

Alternatively, the addKnownGrafanaDataTypes can add these types.

The function is defined in the code, but it does nothing. It will be removed once Thruk API changes are made.

```go
func addKnownGrafanaDataTypes(qm *queryModel, meta *thrukMetadata) {

	findAndChangeType := func(meta *thrukMetadata, name string, t data.FieldType) {
		for i := range meta.Columns {
			if meta.Columns[i].Name == name {
				meta.Columns[i].GrafanaDataType = t
			}
		}
	}

	switch qm.Table {
	case "/services/totals":
		findAndChangeType(meta, "ok", data.FieldTypeInt64)
		findAndChangeType(meta, "warning", data.FieldTypeInt64)
		findAndChangeType(meta, "unknown", data.FieldTypeInt64)
		findAndChangeType(meta, "critical", data.FieldTypeInt64)
	}
}
```
